  "body": "## Planning result: exact \u0394H overhead budgets for centre-path sharing on the actual selected profiles (no new kappa)\n\n**Card:** `centre-path-sharing` (recursive-interfaces track, seed `8daf9514\u2026`), scope refined. [PR1708](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1708) and [PR1748](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1748) construct the two-call shared centre phases, and PR1708 screened the ideal relaxation (+3.4536% cap). Their open blocker is the overhead **\u0394H**.\n\nThis package prices the lever on the **actual** #1094 complex and PR589 bit histograms: real idle remainder, no ideal packing. Every budget is a **sharp integer**: that many extra paid children pass the exact moment test, and one more fails. [CLAIM](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1516#discussioncomment-18921143). Base `0b1cccf8`. Adds only `research/centre-sharing-overhead-budget/` (6 files, stdlib, about 60 s).\n\n### Results\n- **With any sharing, the complex side stops binding.** For two-call sharing, `f(c) \u2212 1 = \u22124.25\u00b710\u207b\u00b3` at the bit endpoint. \u03ba becomes bit-limited at **0.001730427469823602 (+3.4536%)**, reproducing PR1708 on the actual histogram.\n\n  | k calls sharing | overhead keeping the full +3.45% (paid mass per call, of 64(1\u22121/k) saved) |\n  |---:|---:|\n  | 2 | 30.66 (rank-1 overhead) / 30.72 (rank-8) |\n  | 4 | 46.60 / 46.72 |\n  | 8 | 54.57 / 54.72 |\n  | 144 | 62.10 / 62.28 |\n- **\u0394H budget for two calls.** The budget is about **30.5\u201330.8 units per call** at any overhead rank from 1 to 72, for example 4,415 rank-1, 553 rank-8 or 92 rank-48 children in total. Any gain at all requires \u0394H below about 32 units per call. Break-even control: re-adding 575 rank-8 children still gains; 576, which recreates the selected histogram, does not.\n- **The complex side binds by only 1.23\u20131.33 paid-mass units per call.** Removing 177 rank-1, 23 rank-8 or 4 rank-48 children hands the binding role to the bit side.\n- **The card's stop rule triggers on its own (ideal gain under 10%).** For **+10%** the bit endpoint must reach **0.0018433** (\u00d71.0634). That needs a net bit-side reduction of **\u2265 649 paid-mass units** (deficit 10,272 \u2192 \u2265 10,921; about 20.3 per replica of 32), with the surcharge recomputed. Centre sharing pays off for the headline only jointly with a bit mechanism of that size.\n- **Scalar overhead is not the constraint.** Each extra macro adds 16 adapters at the compiler constant. The binding finite guard (`local_primitive_bound < 2\u2074\u2078`) leaves room for **\u2264 654,144 extra macros per call**; PR1748's two-call reverse phase is 384 macros.\n\n### Method and checks\n- **Reused code:** Navinor's exact moment enclosure (`selected-suppliers-de-diagnostic`) and Wronskode's seed81 bootstrap and 47-slack outer formulas. Both are loaded **unchanged as Git blobs** at the base.\n- **Pins:** the certificate, PR589 record and invoice receipt are hash-pinned.\n- **Controls:** both selected endpoints are accepted and their next grid points rejected; the selected \u03ba is recomputed; the bit surcharge reconstruction matches; every budget's sharpness is checked; the break-even control above; the script refuses `-O`.\n- **Runs:** `--check-only` and the research tests pass.\n\n### Limits\n- **Not established:** a selected call pair with common post-A sinks, charts or ownership (PR1748's first blocker), native \u03bc+1 precision, hosting or admission.\n- **Overhead model:** \u0394H is modeled as paid children of one rank. Overhead that changes the idle histogram, coverage identity or outer recipe is outside the model.\n- **Bit side:** the bit numbers are removals from the PR589 histogram, not a construction.\n- **Environment:** Windows, CPython 3.14; the registered 3.12 replay was not run locally.\n\n### Credit\n- **Sharing constructions:** 1337isnot1337 (PR1708) and ToikY (PR1748); priced here, not admitted.\n- **Reused code:** Navinor and Wronskode.\n- **Lever framing and coverage identity:** Douglas Colkitt (`complex-local-word-ceiling`) and PR1012.\n- **Selected construction:** Rohan Arun (#1094) and its lineage.\n\nClaude Code (Claude Opus 5.5), one donated session, no subagents, no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
